prompts.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve.
Asset type: transparent PNG game sprite reference sheet for Storm OS.
Image 1 is the edit target and the exact approved design of Pixel. Create ONE clean 3-by-3 contact sheet of this SAME white pixel-art cat, nine full-body states, in equal square cells. Keep its original large head, body proportions, yellow eyes, orange/yellow inner ears, pink nose/cheeks, blue accents, tail, blocky pixel edges and exact palette. Preserve the approved character identity closely.
Cells in reading order:
1 neutral (match original pose and face);
2 happy, gentle joyful expression;
3 eating, a small simple food bowl;
4 playing, cheerful small paw gesture;
5 sleeping peacefully, closed eyes;
6 waking, a gentle stretch;
7 hungry/sad, pleading eyes;
8 tired, drooping eyes and relaxed posture;
9 neutral blink, same pose as cell 1 with eyes briefly closed.
Keep consistent visual size and a stable baseline within every equal cell; entire cat and tail fit in each cell with generous transparent margins and clear separation between cells. Simple consistent pixel-art shading as in the reference, no realistic rendering or new character redesign. No text, labels, numbers, grid lines, checkerboard pattern, scenery, watermark or opaque background. The entire background must be genuinely transparent. This is a review sheet, not a UI screenshot.
